-- title:
--   Left translates preserve factorizable bi-finite test functions
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and let $\mathrm{tys}$ be an archimedean type family for $F$: data consisting of a natural number $\mathrm{card}\,w$ for each infinite place $w$ and, for each $i < \mathrm{card}\,w$, a type at $w$, namely a dimension $n$ together with a complex representation of `rowIsometrySubgroup₀ w.Completion` on $\mathbb{C}^n$. Let $f$ be a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $F$ which is a factorizable test function, i.e. there are $f_\infty$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles and $f_{\mathrm{fin}}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles with $f_\infty$ given by a $C^\infty$ function of the archimedean matrix entries and compactly supported, $f_{\mathrm{fin}}$ locally constant and compactly supported, and $f(g) = f_\infty(\mathrm{glArch}\,g)\,f_{\mathrm{fin}}(\mathrm{glFin}\,g)$ for all $g$; assume further that $f$ is archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}$, that is, $x \mapsto f(x^{-1})$ lies in $\bigsqcap_w \bigvee_i$ `archTypeSubmoduleAt F w (tys.rep w i)` and $f$ lies in the corresponding infimum of suprema of the submodules `archDualTypeSubmoduleAt F w (tys.rep w i)`. Let $g$ lie in the kernel of `glArch`, so $g$ has trivial archimedean component, and let $k$ lie in the subgroup generated by the ranges of the inclusions `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w`, $w$ ranging over the infinite places. Then the left translate $z \mapsto f((gk)^{-1} z)$ is again a factorizable test function and is again archimedean bi-finite of type $\mathrm{tys}$.
--
--   This is the stability of the space of archimedean bi-finite factorizable test functions under left translation by elements that are purely finite-adelic times elements of the connected archimedean row-isometry groups. It is used in the analysis of cuspidal constituents, in the results bounding infima of cusp subrepresentations intersected with invariants and with the archimedean cut, and in the dichotomy for principal cusp constituents.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_isFactorizableTestFn_comp_inv_mul.lean

